  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "If ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{64}$ is a sample of size $n=64$ drawn from a population with mean $\\mu =10$ and variance ${\\sigma }^{2}=16,$ calculate the value of $\\text{Var}[\\overset{―}{X}].$",
  "worked_solution": "If ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ is a sample of size $n$ from a population with population mean $\\mu $ and population variance ${\\sigma }^{2},$ then\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\mu ,\\,\\text{Var}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\frac{{\\sigma }^{2}}{n}.\n$$\n\nSince the population variance ${\\sigma }^{2}=16$ and the sample size $n=64,$ we have that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[\\overset{―}{X}] & =\\frac{16}{64} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =0.25.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
